---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import FreebieForm from "../../components/FreebieForm.astro";

const CHECKOUT = "https://links.thedigitalincomeedit.com/shop/e7555c8f-7348-4ab4-99ce-0569d6dd0839";
---
<PageLayout
  wide
  title="Pretty & Paid PLR Vault™"
  description="Pretty & Paid PLR Vault™ — a stocked library of done-for-you digital products, licensed to rebrand and sell as your own. $11/month. What you download is yours permanently."
>
  <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
  <section class="v-hero">
    <div class="page-eyebrow">Digital Product Library · Monthly Subscription</div>
    <h1>Pretty &amp; Paid PLR Vault™</h1>
    <p class="lede">A stocked library of done-for-you digital products — designed, licensed, and ready to rebrand and sell as your own. What you download is yours permanently.</p>
    <div class="v-cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href={CHECKOUT}>Open the Vault — $11/month <span class="a">→</span></a>
      <a class="v-link" href="#preview">See inside first →</a>
    </div>
    <ul class="v-trust">
      <li>Instant access</li>
      <li>Full PLR resell license</li>
      <li>Downloads yours to keep — even after you cancel</li>
      <li>20 new products every month</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ PROBLEM ============ -->
  <section class="v-sec">
    <div class="v-kicker">The Real Bottleneck</div>
    <h2>The part nobody warns you about isn't selling. It's everything before selling.</h2>
    <p class="v-intro">Most women who want to sell digital products never get to the selling part. They stall weeks earlier, at one of four gates.</p>
    <div class="v-grid-4">
      <div class="v-gate">
        <span class="v-num">01</span>
        <h3>No product</h3>
        <p>You know planners and guides sell. You've watched other people sell them. But designing one from a blank Canva page is a different job entirely — and it's the job that eats the month.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-gate">
        <span class="v-num">02</span>
        <h3>No shop</h3>
        <p>Etsy, Stan Store, Beacons — each has its own setup logic. Figuring it out from scattered tutorials means forty-seven half-relevant videos and a shop that's still not live.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-gate">
        <span class="v-num">03</span>
        <h3>Nothing to post</h3>
        <p>The shop finally exists — and now it needs content. Reels, Pins, carousels, stories. A second full-time production job stacked on top of the first.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-gate">
        <span class="v-num">04</span>
        <h3>No idea how to make a listing convert</h3>
        <p>The title, the tags, the description, the mockups. The part where good products die quietly because nobody could find them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="v-close">Any one of these can hold a shop closed for months. Most people are stuck at all four at once.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ TRANSFORMATION ============ -->
  <section class="v-sec v-tint">
    <div class="v-kicker">What Changes</div>
    <h2>Imagine skipping straight to the part where you're selling.</h2>
    <p>The Vault collapses those four gates into one afternoon. You open a finished product, restyle it in Canva with your colors and your brand name, follow the listing training for your platform, generate your title, description, tags and mockup prompts in minutes — then post from a content library that's already made.</p>
    <p>Not "learn to design." Not "figure it out eventually." A shop, stocked and live, built from inventory that already exists.</p>
    <p>The work that's genuinely yours — your niche, your brand, your storefront — stays yours. The work that's identical for everyone — the design hours, the template building, the blank-screen listing copy — is already done.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ OVERVIEW ============ -->
  <section class="v-sec">
    <div class="v-kicker">What It Is</div>
    <h2>One subscription. Four problems handled.</h2>
    <p>Pretty &amp; Paid PLR Vault™ is a standalone $11/month subscription — a working inventory system for women building faceless digital product shops. The products, the marketing content, the platform training, and an AI listing tool, in one place.</p>
    <p>It isn't a course. There's nothing to "complete." It's a stocked room, and the subscription is the key.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ INCLUDED ============ -->
  <section class="v-sec">
    <div class="v-kicker">Everything Included</div>
    <h2>What's inside the Vault</h2>

    <div class="v-card">
      <span class="v-num">01</span>
      <h3>The Products</h3>
      <p>Planners. Journals. Guides. eBooks. Printables. Coloring page sets. All fully designed, all editable in Canva. Open the file, swap in your colors, fonts and branding, and list it. Every product carries a full PLR license — rebrand it, customize it, sell it, keep what you earn.</p>
      <p>One download is rarely one file. These are bundles: 30-page guides, 50-plus template sets, reel packs a hundred deep.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="v-card">
      <span class="v-num">02</span>
      <h3>The Content</h3>
      <p>The products come with the marketing to sell them, so launch day never opens on a blank feed.</p>
      <ul class="v-chips">
        <li>Faceless Reel packs</li>
        <li>Stock photo sets</li>
        <li>AI influencer image packs</li>
        <li>Pinterest templates</li>
        <li>Carousel post templates</li>
        <li>Engagement stories</li>
        <li>Announcement post sets</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="v-card">
      <span class="v-num">03</span>
      <h3>The Training</h3>
      <p>Setup walkthroughs for Etsy, Stan Store, Beacons and Canva rebranding — the exact platform mechanics, taught in order, in one place. No stitching together random tutorials.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="v-card v-card-feature">
      <span class="v-num">04</span>
      <h3>PLR Glow Studio</h3>
      <p>An AI tool built into the Vault. Tell it what you're listing and it returns:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Four branded mockup prompts</li>
        <li>An SEO-optimized product title</li>
        <li>A full product description</li>
        <li>SEO tags</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The listing work that stalls most shops for hours is done in minutes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="v-callout">
      <h3>The library you join is the smallest it will ever be</h3>
      <p><strong>20 brand-new products are added every month.</strong></p>
    </div>

    <div class="v-callout v-callout-gold">
      <h3>Yours to keep — permanently</h3>
      <p>Full PLR license to rebrand, customize and sell — and that license survives your subscription. Cancel next year and every file you've downloaded stays yours. The membership is a key to the room, not a lease on what you carry out of it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ HOW IT WORKS ============ -->
  <section class="v-sec v-tint">
    <div class="v-kicker">How It Works</div>
    <h2>Download. Rebrand. List. Sell.</h2>
    <div class="v-steps">
      <div class="v-step"><span class="v-num">01</span><h3>Download</h3><p>Pick a product bundle from the library.</p></div>
      <div class="v-step"><span class="v-num">02</span><h3>Rebrand</h3><p>Open it in Canva. Your colors, your fonts, your name. The rebranding training walks you through it.</p></div>
      <div class="v-step"><span class="v-num">03</span><h3>List</h3><p>Run it through PLR Glow Studio for your title, description, tags and mockups. Follow the setup training for your platform.</p></div>
      <div class="v-step"><span class="v-num">04</span><h3>Sell</h3><p>Post from the content packs. Keep everything you earn.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ PREVIEW / GATED FREEBIE ============ -->
  <section class="v-sec" id="preview">
    <div class="v-kicker">A Real Look</div>
    <h2>Not a description. The actual thing.</h2>
    <p>Before you decide, look inside. The five-page sneak peek shows ten real previews — actual screenshots of actual files, straight out of the Vault.</p>
    <p class="v-note">Each preview is a single example. The sets they come from run thirty, fifty, a hundred pieces deep. You download the whole set, not the sample.</p>
    <FreebieForm heading="Send me the free look inside the Vault" button="Send the Preview" />
  </section>

  <!-- ============ WHO IT'S FOR ============ -->
  <section class="v-sec">
    <div class="v-kicker">Fit</div>
    <h2>Who it's for — and who it isn't</h2>
    <div class="v-grid-2">
      <div class="v-fit">
        <h3>This is for you if</h3>
        <ul class="v-yes">
          <li>You want to sell digital products and have nothing to sell yet</li>
          <li>You'd rather rebrand professional designs than build from blank pages</li>
          <li>You're building faceless — the content packs assume no face on camera</li>
          <li>You want your shop stocked this month, not this quarter</li>
          <li>You can open Canva and change a color</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="v-fit">
        <h3>This isn't for you if</h3>
        <ul class="v-no">
          <li>You want to learn to design original products from scratch — that's education, and the Vault doesn't teach it</li>
          <li>You're looking for coaching, courses or a community — the Vault contains none of those. It contains inventory.</li>
          <li>You expect exclusive files no one else has — PLR means other members download the same source files. Your rebrand is what makes yours yours.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="v-close">Turning away the wrong buyer is worth more than the sale. If you read that second column and felt it, better you know here than on a refund request.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
  <section class="v-sec v-tint">
    <div class="v-kicker">Questions</div>
    <h2>Frequently asked</h2>

    <details class="v-faq"><summary>Is the Vault included in the membership?</summary>
      <p>No. Pretty &amp; Paid PLR Vault™ is its own $11/month subscription. Premium and VIP members don't receive it, and Vault subscribers don't receive membership access. They're two separate things that happen to pair well.</p></details>

    <details class="v-faq"><summary>The membership is $9 and this is $11. Is the Vault just the upgraded membership?</summary>
      <p>No — and this question comes up enough that it's worth answering properly. The prices landing two dollars apart is a coincidence, not a hierarchy. The membership is education: it teaches you to build products, write emails, run ads, grow on Pinterest. The Vault is inventory: it hands you finished products to rebrand and sell. Neither is a version of the other. If you want to learn, the membership. If you want stock, the Vault. If you want both, both — in whichever order suits you.</p></details>

    <details class="v-faq"><summary>What happens to my downloads if I cancel?</summary>
      <p>Nothing. They're yours permanently, license included. You can rebrand and sell products you downloaded during your subscription for as long as you like. Canceling closes the door on new downloads — it never takes back what's already on your computer.</p></details>

    <details class="v-faq"><summary>What exactly does the PLR license let me do?</summary>
      <p>Rebrand the products, customize them, and sell them as your own, keeping what you earn. It's a full private label rights license.</p></details>

    <details class="v-faq"><summary>Can I subscribe to the Vault without joining the community?</summary>
      <p>Yes. That's a completely normal way to use it.</p></details>

    <details class="v-faq"><summary>Do I need design skills?</summary>
      <p>No. Everything opens in Canva as an editable template, and the rebranding training covers the workflow. If you can change a font, you can rebrand a product.</p></details>

    <details class="v-faq"><summary>Which should I start with — the Vault or the membership?</summary>
      <p>Whichever one answers the question you're actually asking. "I have nothing to sell" → the Vault. "I don't know how to sell" → the membership. If you're asking "which is better value," you're comparing two things that don't compete.</p></details>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ PRICING ============ -->
  <section class="v-sec">
    <div class="v-kicker">The Price</div>
    <h2>$11/month. Everything above.</h2>

    <div class="v-price-clarity">
      <p><strong>$11/month. A separate subscription.</strong></p>
      <p>Pretty &amp; Paid PLR Vault™ bills on its own. It is not included in Free, Premium, or VIP membership — and membership is not included in this.</p>
      <p><strong>Yes, the membership is $9 and this is $11. No, this isn't the upgraded version of it.</strong> They're unrelated products that happen to land two dollars apart. The membership teaches you to build. The Vault hands you the stock. You can have either, both, or neither, in any order.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="v-price-box">
      <div class="v-price-fig">$11<span>/month</span></div>
      <ul class="v-price-list">
        <li>The full product library — planners, journals, guides, eBooks, printables, coloring pages</li>
        <li>All marketing content packs — reels, stock photos, AI influencer images, Pinterest, carousels, stories</li>
        <li>Platform training — Etsy, Stan Store, Beacons, Canva rebranding</li>
        <li>PLR Glow Studio</li>
        <li>20 new products every month</li>
        <li>Full PLR license on everything you download — permanently</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn" href={CHECKOUT}>Open Pretty &amp; Paid PLR Vault™ <span class="a">→</span></a>
      <p class="v-fine">Cancel anytime. Your downloads and your license stay yours.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FINAL CTA ============ -->
  <section class="v-final">
    <h2>You could spend another month deciding what to sell. Or you could stock the shop today.</h2>
    <p>The products are designed. The content is made. The training is recorded. The listing tool is waiting. The only piece the Vault can't supply is the decision.</p>
    <a class="btn" href={CHECKOUT}>Open Pretty &amp; Paid PLR Vault™ — $11/month <span class="a">→</span></a>
    <p class="v-fine"><a href="#preview">Still deciding? Take the free look inside first →</a></p>
  </section>

  <p style="margin-top:60px"><a href="/shop" style="color:var(--pink);font-weight:500">← Back to the Shop</a></p>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .v-hero{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto 20px}
  .v-cta-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:8px 0 34px}
  .v-link{color:var(--pink);font-weight:500;font-size:15px}
  .v-trust{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px}
  .v-trust li{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--taupe-deep);
    border:1px solid var(--gray);border-radius:100px;padding:8px 16px;margin:0}

  .v-sec{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:78px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--gray)}
  .v-sec.v-tint{background:var(--cream-deep);border-radius:var(--r);padding:70px 48px;margin:78px auto;border-top:none}
  .v-kicker{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:2.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--pink);margin-bottom:18px}
  .v-sec h2{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,40px);line-height:1.15;
    letter-spacing:-.4px;margin:0 0 26px;max-width:20ch}
  .v-sec h3{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:400;font-size:21px;margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.25}
  .v-intro{font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-size:20px;color:var(--taupe-deep);margin-bottom:36px}
  .v-close{font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-size:19px;color:var(--choc-soft);margin-top:34px}
  .v-note{font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-size:18px;color:var(--taupe-deep)}

  .v-num{display:block;font-family:var(--display);font-size:13px;letter-spacing:2px;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:12px}

  .v-grid-4{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:28px}
  .v-gate{background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--gray);border-radius:var(--r);padding:30px}
  .v-gate p{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;margin:0}

  .v-card{background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--gray);border-radius:var(--r);padding:34px 36px;margin-bottom:22px}
  .v-card p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:14px}
  .v-card p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .v-card-feature{border-color:var(--pink-soft);background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--rose) 0%,var(--white) 62%)}

  .v-chips{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:14px 0 0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:9px}
  .v-chips li{margin:0;font-size:14px;background:var(--blush);border-radius:100px;padding:8px 16px;color:var(--choc-soft)}

  .v-callout{border-left:3px solid var(--pink);background:var(--blush);border-radius:0 14px 14px 0;padding:26px 30px;margin-top:26px}
  .v-callout h3{margin-bottom:8px}
  .v-callout p{margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7}
  .v-callout-gold{border-left-color:var(--gold);background:var(--cream-deep)}

  .v-steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:24px}
  .v-step p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;margin:0}

  .v-grid-2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:34px}
  .v-fit ul{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0}
  .v-fit li{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;margin-bottom:14px;padding-left:28px;position:relative}
  .v-yes li::before{content:"✓";position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--pink);font-weight:600}
  .v-no li::before{content:"✕";position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--taupe);font-weight:600}

  .v-faq{border-bottom:1px solid var(--gray);padding:20px 0}
  .v-faq summary{cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--display);font-size:18px;font-weight:400;list-style:none;
    display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:flex-start}
  .v-faq summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
  .v-faq summary::after{content:"+";color:var(--pink);font-size:22px;line-height:1;flex-shrink:0}
  .v-faq[open] summary::after{content:"–"}
  .v-faq p{margin:16px 0 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--choc-soft)}

  .v-price-clarity{background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--pink-soft);border-radius:var(--r);padding:30px 34px;margin-bottom:32px}
  .v-price-clarity p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:14px}
  .v-price-clarity p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}

  .v-price-box{background:var(--choc);color:var(--cream);border-radius:var(--r);padding:46px 44px;text-align:center}
  .v-price-fig{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:300;font-size:60px;line-height:1;margin-bottom:8px}
  .v-price-fig span{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:16px;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--taupe)}
  .v-price-list{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:26px auto 32px;max-width:520px;text-align:left}
  .v-price-list li{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:13px;padding-left:22px;position:relative;color:var(--cream)}
  .v-price-list li::before{content:"—";position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--gold)}
  .v-fine{font-size:13.5px;color:var(--taupe);margin:18px 0 0}

  .v-final{max-width:760px;margin:80px auto 0;text-align:center;padding-top:70px;border-top:1px solid var(--gray)}
  .v-final h2{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,40px);line-height:1.15;margin:0 auto 22px;max-width:22ch}
  .v-final p{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:30px}
  .v-final .v-fine a{color:var(--pink)}

  @media(max-width:820px){
    .v-grid-4,.v-grid-2{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .v-steps{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
    .v-sec.v-tint{padding:52px 26px}
  }
  @media(max-width:520px){
    .v-steps{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .v-card{padding:26px 24px}
    .v-price-box{padding:34px 24px}
  }
</style>
